# Egress DENYLIST for sandbox-net (tinyproxy.conf: FilterDefaultDeny No, FilterExtended On).
# A sandboxed agent browses the open web like a person would, so public hosts are allowed by
# default; every line here is a POSIX extended regex matched against the request host and a
# match is BLOCKED. The goal: nothing on the compose networks or any private range is
# reachable from a sandbox. Only ports 80/443 leave at all (ConnectPort in tinyproxy.conf).
#
# To go back to a strict allowlist: set FilterDefaultDeny Yes and list the allowed hosts here.

# Single-label names: localhost and every compose service (core, postgres, pgbouncer, valkey,
# agent-runtime, sandbox-gateway, doc-renderer, egress-proxy, caddy, prometheus, grafana ...).
^[^.]+$

# Internal / special-use suffixes.
^(.*\.)?(localhost|local|internal|intranet|lan|home|corp|arpa|test|invalid|example)$

# IPv6 literals (bracketed or bare), and IPv4-mapped forms.
^\[?[0-9a-f]*:[0-9a-f:.]*\]?$

# Private, loopback, link-local, CGNAT, "this network", multicast and reserved IPv4 ranges.
^(0|10|127)\.[0-9]+\.[0-9]+\.[0-9]+$
^169\.254\.[0-9]+\.[0-9]+$
^172\.(1[6-9]|2[0-9]|3[01])\.[0-9]+\.[0-9]+$
^192\.168\.[0-9]+\.[0-9]+$
^100\.(6[4-9]|[7-9][0-9]|1[01][0-9]|12[0-7])\.[0-9]+\.[0-9]+$
^(22[4-9]|2[3-5][0-9])\.[0-9]+\.[0-9]+\.[0-9]+$

# Non-dotted IP spellings (decimal, hex, octal) that resolve to the ranges above.
^[0-9]+$
^0x[0-9a-f]+$
^0[0-7]+(\.[0-7]+)*$

# Cloud metadata endpoints.
^metadata\.google\.internal$
^metadata$
^instance-data$

# --- Add project-specific blocked hosts below this line. One POSIX extended regex per line. ---
